{"archetypes":[{"name":"telemetry-ledger","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff adds a new timing-ledger row type and JSON aggregation path where schema drift or interval matching bugs could silently corrupt reports.","prompt_body":"Investigate the new round timing ledger schema, record-round validation, duration clamping, and timing-report attachment logic. Pay close attention to 13-column TSV compatibility, skill and step matching, and whether rounds attach only to the intended parent interval. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"handoff-state","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Deferred MAV and coder handoff timing depends on persisted state across shell scripts and skill prompt branches.","prompt_body":"Review the implement and design main-agent handoff paths for correct persistence and reuse of round-start timestamps, post-adjudication tally refresh, and best-effort telemetry emission. Check both successful resume and terminal stall exits so handoff wall time and counts are not dropped or double-recorded. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"artifact-publish","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Design publishing now manipulates timing-report-final artifacts where stale sidecars or ordering mistakes could leak incorrect run logs.","prompt_body":"Examine the design publish flow for fresh timing JSON rendering, stale timing-report-final sidecar cleanup, atomic movement, and warning behavior on render failure. Verify the publish ordering cannot copy stale or transient stderr artifacts into committed run logs. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"awk-json","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The report renderer appears to build nested JSON in awk, which is prone to comma, escaping, and array-index mistakes.","prompt_body":"Inspect JSON generation in the timing report renderer, especially nested rounds arrays, comma placement, string escaping, sorting, and child-step interval handling. Look for cases where valid legacy output changes when no round rows exist or where malformed JSON could be emitted with unusual labels or counts. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"bash-portability","focus_area":"code-quality","weight":1,"rationale":"This repository enforces shell harnesses and Bash 3.2 compatibility across many new helper scripts and tests.","prompt_body":"Review the added and modified shell scripts for Bash 3.2 portability, safe quoting, grep and awk portability, subshell side effects, and quiet best-effort failure handling. Focus on whether helpers behave consistently on macOS default tooling and under strict mode. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
